{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790431084,"nonce":"jjyNPwd2Kxa22IBLMjPoWY2J+PA=","title":"A fiber's first call(value) does not bind the function's parameter","message":"In Wren, `Fiber.new { |x| ... }.call(v)` binds `x` to `v` on the first call. WrenLift gets it wrong in every mode:\n\n    var f = Fiber.new { |x| x * 2 }\n    System.print(f.call(21))    // want 42\n\n- interpreter / tiered: `Null does not implement *(_)` (x is null)\n- AOT (native and wasm32): `Fn does not implement *(_)` (x is the closure: the fiber-root call passes the closure as the receiver and the body reads it as its first parameter)\n\nThe AOT fiber-root call in run_fiber_loop passes only the receiver; the value handed to the first call never reaches the body.","files":null}]}